    challenging: "One of you says something breezy about looks, weight or how the other came across at dinner, and the other goes silent for two days. The unbothered one keeps stepping on the same bruise without knowing it exists, then feels accused of cruelty they never intended. The hurt one starts pre-editing outfits and sentences. You two are close enough to reopen an old humiliation and close enough to finally close it. The trap: hinting instead of naming. The move: tell them the exact old story behind the flinch.",
