    challenging: "One of you fits the other's type so exactly that it feels like a setup, and the chosen one gets cast in a role they never auditioned for. The attracted one keeps comparing current behavior to that first-night version and filing complaints when it doesn't match. The other feels loved as an outline and resented as a person. You two argue about 'how you used to be' within the first year. The trap: dating a memory. The move: let them disappoint the fantasy weekly and stay curious anyway.",
