    challenging: "One of you encourages the other a little too much, 'quit the job, it'll work out,' and then isn't around for the fallout. Big promises, weak follow-through. The one being cheered on starts to feel reckless or preached at, and resents both. The trap: optimism used to dodge practical questions. The move: before any big leap, sit down with a notebook, write the worst case and your plan for it, and only then decide.",
